Nightshade is GPLv3. The engine it runs on, Wobbleweed, is MIT, as is the
Hemlock language itself -- so the engine stack stays reusable by anyone,
while the game and everything derived from it stays open.

The GPL binds redistribution by others. It does not bind Schneewolf Labs LLC,
which holds the copyright and may license this code on any terms it chooses,
including linking the official build against proprietary SDKs.

That remains true only while Schneewolf Labs LLC is the sole copyright holder.
The moment an outside contributor's work is merged, they hold copyright in
their contribution, and relicensing -- or granting any exception -- needs their
agreement too. If preserving the ability to relicense matters, adopt a CLA or
DCO BEFORE accepting the first outside pull request. Retrofitting one requires
tracking down every contributor, and that is the step projects usually cannot
complete.

