GOVERNING LAW: Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, United States.

This is recorded here as the entity's choice of law. It is deliberately NOT
written into LICENSE, for two reasons:

1. The GPLv3 text must not be modified. Section 7 enumerates the additional
   terms that may be applied to GPL'd work, and a choice-of-law clause is not
   among them -- adding one would arguably impose a "further restriction" and
   render this project GPL-incompatible, which defeats the purpose of choosing
   copyleft at all.
2. Wobbleweed's MIT is kept verbatim on purpose. "MIT plus extra terms" is
   flagged as a non-standard license by automated scanners and by the legal
   review at any studio evaluating the engine -- which is the precise audience
   MIT was chosen to attract.

Pennsylvania law governs the agreements that actually bind users and
contributors, and that is where the clause belongs:

  - the Terms of Service / EULA for the official servers and the online
    orchestration and account service
  - the Steam distribution and store presence
  - any Contributor License Agreement, if one is adopted (see above -- adopt it
    before the first outside pull request or not at all)
  - the privacy policy covering account data

None of those are the OSS license, and none of them are distributed with the
source, so they carry no copyleft obligation.
